      <p class="pm-eyebrow">How I got here</p>
      <h2>A career built on shipping ambitious work.</h2>
      <div class="pm-timeline">
        <div class="pm-tl">
          <p class="pm-tl__when">Early on</p>
          <h3>Richland, Washington</h3>
          <p>I grew up making backyard movies with friends and taught myself After Effects in 5th grade. I entered student art competitions and earned a spot in independent study programs before high school.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pm-tl">
          <p class="pm-tl__when">Eastern Washington University</p>
          <h3>Film school, and my first crews</h3>
          <p>Four of my short films screened at the Spokane International Film Festival, and I was named “Most Promising Filmmaker.” More importantly, I learned to lead a crew and direct projects end to end.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pm-tl">
          <p class="pm-tl__when">KNDU (NBC affiliate)</p>
          <h3>Creative Services Director</h3>
          <p>I pitched, directed, edited and designed campaigns for local businesses, and directed the station’s first Spanish newscast for Telemundo. I also pitched and solo-produced a docuseries about a championship high school football season that aired on regional TV, barely a year after graduating.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pm-tl">
          <p class="pm-tl__when">Impact Gaming</p>
          <h3>Creative Director</h3>
          <p>I relocated to Las Vegas to join an esports startup, shaping its brand identity and content strategy and producing another docuseries. I wasn’t an esports expert yet. I knew how to build trust and run a project.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pm-tl">
          <p class="pm-tl__when">UFC · four years</p>
          <h3>Post Producer &amp; Motion Designer</h3>
          <p>I produced branded content for UFC’s original content team, worked on long-form programming for Fight Pass and ESPN, and helped market record-breaking Pay-Per-View events, in one of the fastest-paced production environments there is.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pm-tl">
          <p class="pm-tl__when">BoomTV</p>
          <h3>Creative Producer &amp; Animation Director</h3>
          <p>I was asked to lead BoomTV’s video production team, partnering with Fortnite, Halo, Xbox, Mountain Dew, Intel and Sea of Thieves. I shaped creative for 100+ branded events and campaigns, and the work reached 100M+ viewers.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pm-tl">
          <p class="pm-tl__when">AMG (Aftershock Media Group)</p>
          <h3>Project Manager, experiential marketing campaigns</h3>
          <p>I manage experiential marketing campaigns for Activision and
          Devsisters from scope to broadcast. I planned DMZ: Recon’s two-event
          launch (56.6K peak concurrent viewers, 8.3M+ impressions, 52 creators)
          and ran the CookieRun: OvenSmash Creator Crumble broadcast, with 24
          creators streaming live in two formats at once.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pm-tl">
          <p class="pm-tl__when">Today</p>
          <h3>Tiny Pond &amp; In Queue</h3>
          <p>I run my own creative studio, <a href="https://tinypond.studio" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Tiny Pond</a>, and produce esports events through <a href="https://playinqueue.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">In Queue</a>, while taking on freelance work for creators and musicians.</p>
